---
// NOTE (internal): This page and the "ERP Readiness" entry under the Readiness menu
// intentionally point to the same assessment (/readiness/erp). One is the service/approach
// framing for Solutions visitors; the other is the direct diagnostic entry point.
// This overlap is by design -- do not merge or redirect.

import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import HeroText from '~/components/widgets/HeroText.astro';
import Features3 from '~/components/widgets/Features3.astro';
import CallToAction from '~/components/widgets/CallToAction.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: 'ERP Readiness -- OKELAS',
  description:
    'ERP implementations have a well-documented pattern of running over budget and past deadline. OKELAS validates operational logic and cleanses master data before you connect a heavy enterprise system.',
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <HeroText
    tagline="Solutions"
    title="ERP Readiness"
    subtitle="Will this become an expensive, disruptive mess? It's a reasonable fear -- and a solvable one."
  />

  <Features3
    columns={1}
    classes={{ container: 'max-w-3xl' }}
    items={[
      {
        title: 'The problem',
        description:
          'Leadership teams considering ERP are often really asking a narrower question without saying it out loud: "Will this become an expensive, disruptive mess?" It\'s a reasonable fear -- ERP implementations have a well-documented pattern of running over budget and past deadline.',
        icon: 'tabler:alert-circle',
      },
      {
        title: 'Why it happens',
        description:
          'The most consistently cited root cause across ERP industry research isn\'t the software -- it\'s unstandardized process and unclean data going into the new system. An ERP platform automates whatever process you feed it, including a broken one.',
        icon: 'tabler:zoom-question',
      },
      {
        title: 'How OKELAS approaches it',
        description:
          'OKELAS validates operational logic and cleanses master data before you connect a heavy enterprise system -- surfacing the process gaps and data issues that would otherwise turn up mid-implementation, when they\'re far more expensive to fix. This isn\'t a replacement for your ERP vendor or implementation partner; it\'s the readiness work that makes their job succeed.',
        icon: 'tabler:bulb',
      },
      {
        title: 'Quick self-check',
        description:
          'Could you produce a single, agreed answer to "how many SKUs do we have" right now, from one source, without a phone call?',
        icon: 'tabler:checkbox',
      },
    ]}
  />

  <CallToAction
    actions={[
      {
        variant: 'primary',
        text: 'Take the ERP Readiness Assessment',
        href: '/readiness/erp',
        icon: 'tabler:clipboard-check',
      },
    ]}
  >
    <Fragment slot="title">Next step</Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="subtitle">
      Find out exactly where your process and data gaps are before committing to an ERP project.
    </Fragment>
  </CallToAction>
</Layout>
